---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Sterile Processing Compliance & Survey Readiness Software | Certivue"
  description="Stay survey-ready year-round. Certivue keeps SPD competencies, certifications, and training documented and audit-ready for Joint Commission and other surveys."
  canonical="https://certivue.com/compliance"
>
  <section style="padding-top:140px; padding-bottom:64px; padding-left:20px; padding-right:20px;">
    <div style="max-width:760px; margin:0 auto;">
      <h1 style="color:#fff; font-size:clamp(32px, 6vw, 48px); font-weight:500; letter-spacing:-1px; line-height:1.15; margin:0 0 20px;">
        Sterile Processing Compliance &amp; Survey Readiness Software
      </h1>
      <p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.5); font-size:17px; line-height:1.6; margin:0;">
        Surveys don't wait for you to get organized. Certivue keeps your sterile processing department's competencies, certifications, and training documented and audit-ready every day of the year — so a surveyor's request is a two-minute answer, not a two-week fire drill.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section style="padding:0 20px 80px;">
    <div style="max-width:760px; margin:0 auto; display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:48px;">

      <div>
        <h2 style="color:#fff; font-size:26px; font-weight:500; margin:0 0 12px; letter-spacing:-0.3px;">
          Survey readiness is a year-round problem
        </h2>
        <p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.5); font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0;">
          Whether it's The Joint Commission, DNV, or a state inspection, the questions are the same: prove your staff are competent, prove their certifications are current, and prove your training happened. Departments that scramble to assemble this the week before a survey are the ones that get findings. The departments that pass treat readiness as something they maintain continuously.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 style="color:#fff; font-size:26px; font-weight:500; margin:0 0 12px; letter-spacing:-0.3px;">
          Competency documentation, always current
        </h2>
        <p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.5); font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0;">
          Every competency assessment in Certivue is timestamped, attributed to an assessor, and graded on a defined scale — with failing results kept open for retraining rather than quietly closed. When a surveyor asks whether a technician was assessed on a specific process, the record is already there.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 style="color:#fff; font-size:26px; font-weight:500; margin:0 0 12px; letter-spacing:-0.3px;">
          Certifications that never lapse unnoticed
        </h2>
        <p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.5); font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0;">
          Certivue tracks CRCST, CBSPD, CIS, CHL, and other credentials with expiration monitoring and stored certificate documents, plus a role-based view of where the whole department stands. Lapsed certifications surface before they become findings, not after.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 style="color:#fff; font-size:26px; font-weight:500; margin:0 0 12px; letter-spacing:-0.3px;">
          Training you can prove
        </h2>
        <p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.5); font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0;">
          Assign in-services to your staff, attach the supporting documentation, and build a continuous education history for every technician. The evidence lives with the record, so proving training happened takes one click.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 style="color:#fff; font-size:26px; font-weight:500; margin:0 0 12px; letter-spacing:-0.3px;">
          One source of truth when the surveyor arrives
        </h2>
        <p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.5); font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0;">
          Instead of pulling binders from three cabinets and cross-checking spreadsheets, your competency, certification, and training records live in one system, organized by employee and by department. Survey prep stops being an event and becomes something you're always ready for.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div style="text-align:center; background:#161820; border:0.5px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); border-radius:12px; padding:48px;">
        <h2 style="color:#fff; font-size:26px; font-weight:500; margin:0 0 10px; letter-spacing:-0.3px;">
          Get survey-ready with Certivue
        </h2>
        <p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.5); font-size:15px; margin-bottom:28px;">
          See how sterile processing departments stay audit-ready year-round.
        </p>
        <a
          href="/#demo"
          style="display:inline-block; background:#22d3c8; color:#0f1117; font-weight:500; border-radius:8px; padding:10px 22px; text-decoration:none; font-size:15px;"
        >
          Request a demo
        </a>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
